1
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Sometimes love is stranger than fiction.

2
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Watching the Detectives is a comedy, romance film directed by Paul Soter.

3
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Neil, a self-proclaimed film geek and owner of Gumshoe video, has always been
content to live vicariously through his favorite films noir.

4
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:10,000
But when he meets Violet, a real-life femme fatale, his mundane world gets turned upside
down and the line between reality and the movies quickly begins to blur.

5
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Neil, played by Cillian Murphy.

6
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Violet, played by Lucy Liu.

7
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:58,000
Jonathan, played by Jason Sudeikis.

8
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:14,000
Lucien, played by Michael Panes.

9
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
Marcia, played by Callie Thorne.

10
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
Buddy, played by Michael Yurchak.

11
01:08:56,000 --> 01:09:02,000
Watching the Detectives is a 2007 American romantic comedy film written and
directed by Paul Soter in his feature directorial debut.

12
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
The film stars Cillian Murphy as the film geek owner of an independent video rental store
whose life is upended when he meets a thrill-seeking femme fatale (Lucy Liu).

13
01:21:28,000 --> 01:21:34,000
The film had its world premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival on May 1, 2007,
and was released on DVD in the United States on August 12, 2008.

14
01:27:44,000 --> 01:27:50,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark and emotional.
